From 89e9a7e10094dfc5f893341a633ee9436e0c8d80 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Saikrishna Edupuganti <6157640+krsna1729@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:35:11 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fib: fix table overwrite on wrap at end of address space

When a route is added or deleted, modify_fib() walks the more specific
routes it covers and moves a left edge past each one. If those routes
run contiguously up to 255.255.255.255, stepping past the last one
wraps the left edge to 0. The branch taken when the left edge is
already at the next covered route does not check for the wrap. The
final range check no longer stops the walk either, since it skips a
left edge of 0 (for the default route added first), so the walk ends
in install_to_fib(dp, 0, 0, nh): the next hop is written over the
whole address space. An add leaves every tbl24 entry with the added
route's next hop; a delete leaves every entry with the covering
route's next hop, or the default next hop.

The common case is a change to the default route while the routes
under it reach the top of the space contiguously: 0.0.0.0/1 and
128.0.0.0/1 (as VPN clients install over a default), or 224.0.0.0/4
and 240.0.0.0/4. Adding, re-pointing or deleting 0.0.0.0/0 then makes
every lookup return the default route's new next hop, or the default
next hop. Any prefix ending at 255.255.255.255 behaves the same. With
10.0.0.0/8 -> 7, 255.255.255.254/32 -> 1 and 255.255.255.255/32 -> 2,
adding 255.255.255.254/31 -> 3 makes every lookup, 10.1.2.3 included,
return 3.

Commit ab1b927cd73e ("fib: fix adding default route overwriting entire
table") added the wrap check after an installed range only. Add the
same check to the branch that skips an empty range, and a test for
both cases and both operations.

Fixes: 880bc2b5f3bd ("fib: fix adding default route")
Cc: stable@dpdk.org

[BESS: lib/ hunk only; the upstream patch also adds test_wrap_around to
app/test/test_fib.c, made against DPDK main. BESS's reproducers are in
core/route/route_test.cc.]

Upstream-Status: Pending
BESS-Decision: D-132
---
 lib/fib/dir24_8.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lib/fib/dir24_8.c b/lib/fib/dir24_8.c
index 489d2ef427..5a47b76875 100644
--- a/lib/fib/dir24_8.c
+++ b/lib/fib/dir24_8.c
@@ -436,6 +436,12 @@ modify_fib(struct dir24_8_tbl *dp, struct rte_rib *rib, uint32_t ip,
 			if (ledge == redge) {
 				ledge = redge +
 					(uint32_t)(1ULL << (32 - tmp_depth));
+				/*
+				 * we got to the end of address space
+				 * and wrapped around
+				 */
+				if (ledge == 0)
+					break;
 				continue;
 			}
 			ret = install_to_fib(dp, ledge, redge,
